# Approvals policy: who approves what in this repository (read by lane_guard.py).
# Dalaun's lane: only he changes this file, so no agent pull request can widen it.
#
# Analogy: CODEOWNERS says whose desk a file sits on. This file is the office
# rulebook: which desks the staff may finish work on by themselves (agent lane:
# merges itself once lane-guard, keystone and a Verifier pass are green), which
# need the owner's signature (owner: waits for Dalaun), and which pages may only
# ever get longer (append-only, grows-only).
#
# One rule a line:   <rule>  <path>  <part>  <state>
#
#   rule   agent        the path is in the agent lane
#          owner        the path is in Dalaun's lane (every path is, unless an agent line takes it out)
#          append-only  the file may only gain lines at its end (history is never rewritten)
#          grows-only   the file, or one top-level function of it (<part>), may only gain lines:
#                       an agent may add a check, never change or remove one
#   path   "/dir/" for a folder, "/path/file" for one file (no wildcards)
#   part   a function name for grows-only, "-" otherwise
#   state  enforce      the lane guard acts on it
#          observe      the lane guard only reports what it would do (step summary,
#                       a notice, and one comment on the pull request when the answer
#                       differs). Nothing waits on an observe rule.
#
# For agent and owner lines the last matching line wins (GitHub's CODEOWNERS rule).
# append-only and grows-only lines add a condition to an agent-lane file; they
# never move a file into the agent lane.
#
# The enforce agent and owner lines must match .github/CODEOWNERS line for line,
# or the lane guard's own cases fail and every pull request waits for Dalaun.
# To switch an observe owner line on: change "observe" to "enforce" here and add
# the same path to CODEOWNERS with @dalaun, in one pull request.

# ---- Enforced today (the lane as it stood on 2026-11-23) -------------------------
agent        /rehearsal/loop/BACKLOG.md                         -          enforce
agent        /rehearsal/loop/score-ledger.csv                   -          enforce
agent        /rehearsal/loop/NEXT-MOVES.md                      -          enforce
agent        /rehearsal/synthetic/                              -          enforce
owner        /rehearsal/synthetic/structure-cases-facts.json    -          enforce
append-only  /rehearsal/loop/score-ledger.csv                   -          enforce
grows-only   /rehearsal/synthetic/rehearsal_run.py              selftest   enforce
grows-only   /rehearsal/synthetic/synthetic_year.py             main       enforce

# ---- Observe only (added 2026-11-24; reports, never blocks) ----------------------
# The relay's finish line. scorecard.py decides when the relay stops, and the
# grantor check decides whether the Family Trust reads as non-grantor (what
# scorecard SC1 grades). Both sit inside the agent folder above, so today the
# agent that is graded could rewrite its own grader. "Checks, goal and rules stay
# his": these lines would send any change to them to Dalaun.
owner        /rehearsal/synthetic/scorecard.py                  -          observe
owner        /rehearsal/synthetic/grantor_check.py              -          observe
# SC6 reads the "Documents that would clear it" list here, and SC2 checks every
